{
 "version": 1,
 "projectId": "s6adv-trigonometry-and-measure-of-angles-1-trigonometry-with-acute-angles-v1",
 "comments": {
  "e439d21f-fd4e-42bf-8202-832d016ef504": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p3-ratios-block",
     "replacement": "- There are three **trigonometric ratios: sine, cosine, and tangent**, which compare the lengths of two sides of a right-angled triangle.\n- Each ratio refers to a chosen acute angle $\\theta$. The **hypotenuse** is the side opposite the right angle, the **opposite** side faces $\\theta$ and the **adjacent** side touches $\\theta$ but is not the hypotenuse.\n- You can remember the three ratios using SOH CAH TOA.\n\n$\\sin\\theta=\\frac{\\text{Opposite}}{\\text{Hypotenuse}}$\t$\\cos\\theta=\\frac{\\text{Adjacent}}{\\text{Hypotenuse}}$\t$\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\text{Opposite}}{\\text{Adjacent}}$",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p3-ratios-block",
     "targetFingerprint": "188e5b525ca162fdeeb5526ae51fa97c858f97954b4058df4c407ba93eb67d57",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-trigonometry-and-measure-of-angles-1-trigonometry-with-acute-angles-v1/20261111-083532",
   "revision": 16
  },
  "85188b0f-0846-4a9b-836f-ab57128924a3": {
   "kind": "theory-wording",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p9-definition",
     "nodeId": "p9-definition-text",
     "replacement": "Bearings: https://www.geogebra.org/m/er3jqacn\n\n- **Bearings** give a travel direction from one point to another.\n- With bearings, we always take a **top-down view.**\n- **True bearing** is the angle measured clockwise from north.\n- True bearings **always use three digits**, for example $045^{\\circ}$.\n  If a navigator hears only two digits, they know to ask for a repeat.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p9-definition",
     "targetFingerprint": "79691e11abbc3a2852cbc18fd4437a948b66c8d0b05392aaaa831b0dc5bdd1b6",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-trigonometry-and-measure-of-angles-1-trigonometry-with-acute-angles-v1/20261111-083532",
   "revision": 16
  },
